{"name":"Oregano Spice","hex":"#8d8764","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oregano","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A herb of the mint family, Origanum vulgare, having aromatic leaves.","Other herbs with a similar flavor, including other species in the genus Origanum, and Mexican oregano, Lippia graveolens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oregano"},{"term":"spice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Aromatic or pungent plant matter (usually dried) used to season or flavor food.","The quality of being spicy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add spice or spices to; season.","To spice up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oregano","blocks":[{"text":"Oregano, sometimes called wild marjoram, is a species of flowering plant in the mint family, Lamiaceae. It is native to the Mediterranean region but widely naturalised elsewhere in the temperate Northern Hemisphere, particularly the United States and Mexico."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Origanum_vulgare_-_harilik_pune.jpg/330px-Origanum_vulgare_-_harilik_pune.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oregano","wikidata":"Q134283"},{"title":"Spice","blocks":[{"text":"In the culinary arts, a spice is a seed, fruit, root, bark, or other plant substance primarily used for flavouring or colouring food. Spices are distinguished from herbs, which are the leaves, flowers, or stems of plants used for flavouring or as a garnish. Spices and herbs are both seasonings. \nSpices are sometimes used in medicine, religious rituals, cosmetics, or perfume production. They are usually classified into spices, spice seeds, and herbal categories. For example, vanilla is commonly used as an ingredient in fragrance manufacturing. Plant-based sweeteners such as sugar are not considered spices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.